      "markdown": "To distinguish selling-price and quantity effects in revenue changes, calculate realized unit selling prices (qualifying revenue divided by actual units sold) and total unit volumes across comparable periods at the appropriate product grain, rather than relying on catalogue retail prices, order counts, or distinct customer reach. You can then apply a standard price-volume decomposition to evaluate the arithmetic contribution of price changes versus unit volume changes, while accounting for product mix shifts that can alter aggregate average prices even when individual item prices remain unchanged.",
